title: Hide VCS Metadata From Sandboxes
status: draft
created: 2026-11-21
author: Luke Carrier
context: "Litterbox pairs a sandbox with a Git branch and a unit of compute. Today the workspace is always a private copy: `create` calls `vcs.prepare`, materialises the base revision into a `TempDir`, and hands that directory to the backend as `CreateRequest.workspace.source` (`orchestrator/service.rs:140-162`), so the sandbox never sees `.git`. Repair does the same (`service.rs:313-341`).\n\nThe map `maps/2026-11-18-litterbox-vcs-history-sync` settles that a bound workspace is also possible. Its `decision` field describes jj as one workspace per sandbox behind a non-colocated bridge with `.jj` masked. T-002 and T-012 answer how: bubblewrap puts a tmpfs over the metadata path, Docker uses an empty volume at it, the contents are hidden, the directory entry remains empty, and a backend that cannot mask refuses `Bound`. Both tickets are `answered`, so masking is decided rather than open.\n\nThe decouple ADR left the primitives in place. `BindingSupport::{Copied, Bound, Both}` exists (`vcs/capabilities.rs:10-19`), `Vcs::masked_paths` is on the trait (`vcs/mod.rs:39`), and `GitVcs` reports `Copied` with an empty mask (`vcs/git/scm.rs:388-403`). Its EC-007 settled that `prepare` takes no binding argument and that a combination the backend cannot honour is refused when the configuration is validated, before any sandbox is created, and never falls back to copying.\n\nWhat is missing is the choice. `StoredSandbox` carries `sandbox`, `branch_name` and `remote` and no binding (`metadata_store.rs:17-25`). `[git]` is project-owned and holds one key, `snapshot-mode` (`config.rs:54-60`), and `reject_project_keys_in_user` refuses it in the user configuration (`config_loader.rs:310-332`). No backend can mask: bubblewrap emits `--tmpfs` for `/tmp` and `/home` only (`backends/bubblewrap/view.rs:318-321`), Docker sets no `Binds` in `HostConfig` (`backends/docker/compute.rs:192-205`), and Seatbelt's renderer emits only allow rules after `(deny default)` (`backends/seatbelt/policy.rs:173-199`).\n\nThis ADR adds the choice and makes it safe. `CONTEXT.md` now defines **Workspace setting** and **Workspace binding**."
problem: "A sandbox that binds a host workspace directory would read and write `.git` or `.jj` through it. Nothing chooses between a private copy and a bound directory, nothing records the choice per sandbox, no compute backend can mask a metadata path, and no configuration path lets a machine say which it wants for one workspace."
goals[6]:
  - "A sandbox never reads or writes VCS metadata, whichever binding it was created with."
  - "The binding is a workspace setting in the untracked local override, keyed per VCS, with no default."
  - "The binding is recorded per sandbox and honoured by every later operation."
  - "Bubblewrap and Docker can mask a bound workspace."
  - "A backend that cannot mask refuses `Bound` rather than degrading."
  - "A missing key is a configuration error, never a silent copy."
nonGoals[5]:
  - "The VCS selector. `[vcs] tool` and the `[vcs.jj]` section land with the ADR that introduces jj."
  - "Darwin masking. It depends on this configuration wiring and on a probe of Seatbelt's deny-rule ordering, recorded as evidence beside the map, and lands as a separate change written and tested on a macOS host."
  - "The state machine, conflict mechanics and history retention."
  - "Removing `.git` from a copied workspace. `materialise` unpacks an archive, so `.git` is already absent under `Copied`."
  - "Making the directory entry absent rather than empty."
requirements[12]{id,title,slug,description}:
  FR-001,"The binding enum",binding-enum,"`sandbox::contract` owns `WorkspaceBinding` with variants `Copied` and `Bound`, beside `StoreView` and `SnapshotSelector`, because persistence and configuration both need it and arch-lint forbids either from importing `vcs` (`arch-lint.toml:104` and `245`). `BindingSupport` moves there from `vcs::capabilities` so the vocabulary has one home, and `vcs` imports both. The enum has no `Default` impl and no serde default, so a configuration section that omits it is a missing value rather than a silent copy."
  FR-002,"The configuration key",config-key,"A machine-owned `binding` key in the `[vcs.<tool>]` section of the untracked `.agentkit/litterbox/config.local.toml`, accepting `copied` or `bound`. The section mirrors `[backends]`: `ProjectFile` gains an untyped `vcs` map, `Config` gains `vcs_settings`, the committed project file's table is noticed and ignored, and the user configuration is refused. `[git]` is deleted and `snapshot-mode` moves to `[vcs.git]`, so it becomes a workspace setting rather than project configuration. `CONFIG_KEYS` drops `git` and gains `vcs`, and `reject_project_keys_in_user` gains a `vcs` clause."
  FR-003,"No default",no-default,"`create` refuses with a configuration error naming the key, the accepted values and the file when `binding` is absent. There is no fallback to `Copied`."
  FR-004,"The record field",record-field,"`StoredSandbox` gains `binding`, written at create and read by every later operation, so a configuration change affects only new sandboxes."
  FR-005,"Legacy records",legacy-records,"A record written before this change has no binding field. It loads as `Current` and is treated as `Copied`, because that is how it was created. It is never rewritten and is reported as a legacy fact."
  FR-006,"Validation before create",validation,"The selected VCS reports the bindings its configuration can honour, and a combination it cannot honour is refused when the configuration is validated, before any sandbox is created. Git reports `Copied`, so `bound` is refused for Git."
  FR-007,"The mask contract",mask-contract,"`masked_paths` names `.git` and `.jj`. Under `Copied` the backend receives a private copy that excludes them, which `materialise` already guarantees because it unpacks an archive. Under `Bound` the compute backend masks each one."
  FR-008,"Bubblewrap masks",bwrap-masking,"Bubblewrap renders a tmpfs over each masked path inside the bound workspace, so the contents are hidden and the directory entry remains empty."
  FR-009,"Docker masks",docker-masking,"Docker mounts an empty volume at each masked path inside the bound workspace. It refuses `Bound` when it cannot guarantee that the daemon shares the host filesystem, because the bind source is interpreted on the daemon's side."
  FR-010,"A backend that cannot mask refuses",mask-refusal,"A compute backend reports whether it can mask. One that cannot refuses `Bound` with a structured unsupported failure naming the backend, the binding and the remedy. Seatbelt cannot mask today, because its renderer emits no deny rule, so it refuses `Bound`."
  FR-011,"The bound directory",bound-directory,"The VCS backend owns one host directory per bound sandbox, derived from the project slug and sandbox name the way `bubblewrap::workspace::sandbox_directory` derives its state directory. The path is not stored in the record, because the backend recomputes it and a stored path goes stale when the data directory moves."
  FR-012,"Removal and orphans",orphans,"A bound directory is removed with its sandbox. `prune` releases project storage that is no longer needed and is extended to remove bound directories with no record, and its call condition widens from `stored.remote` to also cover a record whose binding is `Bound` (`orchestrator/service.rs:478-482`). A failed create removes the directory on every path that already removes the branch (`service.rs:145-147`, `172-174`, `191-193`)."
nonFunctional[4]{id,title,slug,description}:
  NFR-001,"The project cannot set the binding",project-cannot-set,"The committed project file never carries `binding`, and a configuration that tries is refused or ignored with a notice, matching how `store-view` and `forwarding` are handled (`config.rs:399-419`)."
  NFR-002,"The record decides",record-decides,"Later operations read the binding from the record, never from the current configuration."
  NFR-003,"No silent fallback",no-fallback,"Every refusal names the class, the key or value, the reason and the remedy. No path substitutes `Copied` for a requested `Bound`."
  NFR-004,"The gates run in CI",gates,"`cargo test -p agentkit-litterbox`, `cargo clippy -p agentkit-litterbox --all-targets -- -D warnings`, `arch-lint check` and `bash hack/arch-lint-negative.sh` pass."
acceptance[5]{id,title,slug,description}:
  AC-001,"No VCS data either way",no-vcs-data,"A sandbox created with `Copied` and one created with `Bound` both expose no VCS metadata: `.git` and `.jj` are absent from the copy, or present as an empty directory entry under a mask, and no read or write reaches the VCS."
  AC-002,"A missing key is refused",missing-key-refused,"`create` without `binding` fails with a configuration error naming the key and the file."
  AC-003,"Legacy records load as Copied",legacy-loads,"A record file with no binding field loads as `Current` with `Copied`, and its sandbox still lists, deletes and repairs."
  AC-004,"A backend that cannot mask refuses Bound",cannot-mask-refuses,"A `Bound` request against a backend that cannot mask fails with an unsupported refusal naming the backend and the remedy, and no sandbox is created."
  AC-005,"The gates pass",gates-pass,"`cargo test -p agentkit-litterbox` and `cargo clippy -p agentkit-litterbox --all-targets -- -D warnings` pass, and `arch-lint check` and the negative fixture are unchanged."
edgeCases[6]{id,title,slug,description}:
  EC-001,"The empty mountpoint",empty-mountpoint,"Masking hides the contents and leaves the directory entry. An empty `.git` is not an absent `.git`, and this ADR does not claim absence. T-002 records that absence needs an overlay or whiteout that is unproved on both mechanisms."
  EC-002,"The path is derived, not stored",derived-path,"The bound directory is a function of the project slug and sandbox name. A record does not carry it, so moving the data directory does not orphan a sandbox."
  EC-003,"A failed create leaves no directory",failed-create,"Create removes the bound directory on every path that already removes the branch, including a provisioning failure and a record-store failure."
  EC-004,"A corrupt record leaves an orphan",corrupt-orphan,"A record that cannot be read cannot be addressed, so a forced delete removes the record and the compute state but nothing knows a bound directory existed. `prune` is the only path that finds it."
  EC-005,"Docker's daemon is local",docker-local,"Docker connects over a local unix socket and refuses `tcp://` (`backends/docker/compute.rs:630-667`), so a bind source is read on the daemon's side. A daemon whose filesystem is not the host's cannot honour `Bound` and must refuse it."
  EC-006,"`[git]` fails as an unknown field",old-git-key,"Removing the `git` field from `ProjectFile` makes a configuration that still sets `[git]` fail to parse, because `ProjectFile` derives `deny_unknown_fields`. No migration code is written."
